---
// NOTE: plain-language terms describing how this site operates. Not legal advice
// and not reviewed by a lawyer. Have counsel review before launch.
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../config/site";

const updated = "August 24, 2026";
---

<Page
  title="Terms of Use | VT Dispensary Directory"
  description="Terms governing use of VT Dispensary Directory, including accuracy limits, age restrictions, and the site's relationship to listed dispensaries."
  label="Legal"
  heading="Terms of use"
  intro={`Last updated ${updated}.`}
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Who this is for</h2>
    <p>
      This site is for adults 21 and over. Cannabis is legal for adults 21 and over in
      Vermont. By using the site you confirm you meet that age requirement.
    </p>

    <h2>What we are</h2>
    <p>
      An independent directory. We are not a dispensary, not a delivery service, and not
      affiliated with any listed business. We do not sell cannabis, take orders, process
      payments, or hold inventory. Every transaction happens between you and a licensed
      retailer, on their premises or their website, under their terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy, and its limits</h2>
    <p>
      We verify listings against the Cannabis Control Board's licensee list and each
      dispensary's Google Business Profile, and we date every verification. We still cannot
      guarantee accuracy. Shops move, change hours, close, and rebrand faster than any
      directory refreshes.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where we have not verified something, the listing says so rather than guessing. Call
      ahead before you drive somewhere. If you find something wrong, tell us and we will fix it.
    </p>

    <h2>Not advice</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing here is medical, legal, or financial advice. Strain profiles and guides are
      general reference. If you are managing a health condition, talk to a clinician. If you
      need to know what the law requires of you, read the
      <a href="https://ccb.vermont.gov/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cannabis Control Board</a>
      or talk to a lawyer.
    </p>

    <h2>Federal law</h2>
    <p>
      Cannabis remains illegal under United States federal law regardless of Vermont's rules.
      Among other consequences, transporting cannabis across a state line is a federal offence.
      Nothing on this site should be read as encouraging that.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      We link to dispensary websites and menus, some as affiliate links, explained in the
      <a href="/affiliate/">affiliate disclosure</a>. We do not control those sites and are not
      responsible for their content, their accuracy, or what they do with your data.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not scrape the directory wholesale, republish it as your own, or use it to build a
      competing dataset. Do not attempt to interfere with the site's operation. Reasonable
      personal use, and quoting us with a link, are both fine.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided as-is. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for losses
      arising from reliance on information here, including a wasted trip to a shop that turned
      out to be closed. Verify anything that matters before you act on it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may change. The date at the top reflects the current version.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
